Market Restraints
Patent Expirations and Biosimilar Competition
Patent expirations can expose established oncology medicines to competition from generic drugs and biosimilars, depending on the product and regulatory pathway. This competition may reduce prices and affect revenue for originator companies.

While lower-cost alternatives can improve access to treatment, manufacturers may face greater pressure to differentiate their portfolios, develop next-generation therapies, and maintain market share after the loss of exclusivity.

Affordability and Unequal Access to Treatment
Access to cancer medicines varies across countries and patient groups because of differences in healthcare funding, insurance coverage, medicine availability, and specialist infrastructure. High-cost treatments may remain inaccessible to patients in settings with limited resources.

Supply limitations and gaps in specialized cancer-care services can also affect treatment access. Improving affordability, strengthening healthcare delivery, and expanding the availability of suitable medicines remain important considerations for the market.

